  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2649e1d1dd774de583cc38df96dc94de",
      "statement": "Cite-Right's tokenizer surface is a single `Tokenizer` protocol in `src/cite_right/core/interfaces.py` that exposes `tokenize(text) -> TokenizedText`, is `@runtime_checkable`, and is implemented by `SimpleTokenizer` (default), `HuggingFaceTokenizer`, and `TiktokenTokenizer`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/__init__.py#L65-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c312a5eb8ff3088a04948d2dc89c7cb4c8a6aab7731a54ca0bc7db1cf5a052ee:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/interfaces.py#L10-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4645809795e84f5fae19001d5c4794cca3280c086d9ab7c8f0789ec651542e78:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95c86dd248404522a70197000419eeab",
      "statement": "The `TokenizedText` Pydantic model in `src/cite_right/core/results.py` validates, via `_validate_token_spans`, that `token_ids` and `token_spans` have equal length, that every span stays within `text` bounds with `start < end`, and that spans are monotonic and non-overlapping.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L10-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51a2336af6eab8886895cc657834fb67ae818a3d597450d23eec8a567cf1ac90:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ab5b6e2208754e4f8aa1499982963e7e",
      "statement": "`SimpleTokenizer` in `src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py` is a dependency-free, rule-based default tokenizer that tokenizes by walking the text once, applies Unicode NFKC and case-folding, folds curly-quote and dash variants to ASCII, and returns `TokenizedText` with `token_spans` pointing into the original (unnormalized) text so the citation rebase stays correct.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py#L231-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:003848b9b073650a9ce3b8407ab467b3e028bf2c472bafff0d259e232b31b5fb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py#L66-L147",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:988594c206b140dd71c4fa2933d4e50b614bd3f884b224e3ee67c7c686fe5d55:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_20167034e17241cc98711f21f6f5348d",
      "statement": "`TokenizerConfig` in `src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py` provides three optional normalization knobs on top of `SimpleTokenizer`: `normalize_numbers` (strip `,` from number tokens), `normalize_percent` (map standalone `%` to the word `percent`), and `normalize_currency` (map `$`, `€`, `£` to `dollar`, `euro`, `pound`); all three default to `True`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py#L11-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:46094847b2ba3ce4f5bb14f66c94063ccb4b9ca99477ce39b56e192c3b32cb60:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py#L268-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36cde12652dea2fffa0dbc5c42da7e311d15af01ca7c3691d1e1e258d1f8447f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_11a6fbd650cb412c8a4e759c57cffdb7",
      "statement": "`SimpleTokenizer` builds its vocabulary lazily in `_vocab` and assigns each new normalized token the next `_next_id`; the Rust prepare path overwrites `_vocab` and `_next_id` from `rust_corpus.get_vocab()` so the Python tokenizer's IDs match the inverted index that prepared the corpus.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L198-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1bea82c400b56317c5f3a0e9b93db7164e3ac0581e7fab475e625127e30552c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py#L75-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d8d451aded5daaa858f15f38943bfd0d63f82345fda90d3ccd340598c42a036a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4e800259c29b4566b285260bc9126745",
      "statement": "`HuggingFaceTokenizer` in `src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_huggingface.py` wraps either a `tokenizers.Tokenizer` or a `transformers.PreTrainedTokenizerBase` (discriminated by `_check_tokenizer_type`, raising `TypeError` otherwise), filters out empty-span special tokens, and exposes `from_pretrained` which raises `ImportError` pointing at `cite-right[huggingface]` when `transformers` is not installed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_huggingface.py#L142-L240",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe85fd36b0daf25ea88ce7df530585d95f9aefd026a4672abd54d165df0d825a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_huggingface.py#L26-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92134f187569f8bbc32846a0d745202711d676498f9dc9ea4779da1f4859465e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17435925ceee45a7aa6bd860325c99f9",
      "statement": "`HuggingFaceTokenizer` defaults to `add_special_tokens=False` because `[CLS]`, `[SEP]`, and similar markers have empty character spans and would fail the `TokenizedText` invariant that `start < end`; the fast-tokenizer path also defaults to `use_fast=True`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_huggingface.py#L101-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76f2b908379a9a69aa3e9717cb0bbf0c4fd66eb8c5256f3af6260adac0bf2342:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_huggingface.py#L45-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66e79d0719b5746c97636d5ade05066098cf31a6850e4323b44424192593815d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3cd206fb35e445d6a1ee58ec2d9e1582",
      "statement": "`TiktokenTokenizer` in `src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_tiktoken.py` defaults to the `cl100k_base` encoding (GPT-4, GPT-3.5-turbo, `text-embedding-ada-002`), accepts `p50k_base` (Codex) and `r50k_base` (GPT-3 davinci/curie), and raises `ImportError` pointing at `cite-right[tiktoken]` when `tiktoken` is not installed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_tiktoken.py#L42-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cd415dbff3ef842f79e682e8a6ac16685c88f4d0f0f2867543401430cf22ddec:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_727009f6e2ae421c989e0cf790c29be1",
      "statement": "`TiktokenTokenizer` produces character-accurate spans by building a `byte_to_char` lookup from the UTF-8 byte stream once, then mapping each BPE token's byte range to a character range through that table; it raises `ValueError` if a token maps to a zero-width character span.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer_tiktoken.py#L77-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a70cbe7fb30969d022d300061aa2b237391416c3d115a9be00106d0ea9114ca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec193e877e0643059800b0fd9142853a",
      "statement": "A custom tokenizer (anything other than `SimpleTokenizer`) forces the lexical fallback path: in `PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources`, the Rust prepare path is skipped, `inverted_index` and `rust_corpus` are left as `None`, and `_select_candidates` uses the lexical prefilter over `Candidate.token_set` plus optional embedding extras; Smith-Waterman still localizes on the chosen candidates.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L126-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d2c530df4ff885b3461ca48d574ae56bbd77f733a5f5968df48af05ab689192:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L187-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ebc8b2396396a57f50ce1bbb5c2c56dd456c4fd04fc5fc1c2c74f75a980f1743:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a0c6e33c69814334a9f09ce153a522e3",
      "statement": "`PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources` and `align_citations` accept a `tokenizer` keyword argument in the same place; `align_citations` forwards the tokenizer to `PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources`, so a non-default tokenizer in `align_citations` triggers the same lexical fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L72-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f18addfd72cfa7d4e34677f5e3f485ed2b217e6f119ed2239a42099a3cbbba7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L126-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d2c530df4ff885b3461ca48d574ae56bbd77f733a5f5968df48af05ab689192:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0babe4845b7c4ef981a5c37168a230f3",
      "statement": "The HuggingFace and Tiktoken tokenizers require their respective extras: `pip install \"cite-right[huggingface]==0.4.0\"` and `pip install \"cite-right[tiktoken]==0.4.0\"`.",
